"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th and a Phase One budget of $500,000 led by Sarah Tan. The project team has expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Significant progress has been made in Phase Two, achieving a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report to be shared on November 20th. The design phase has been successfully completed, and the team is moving into the development phase starting next month, guided by lead developer Omar Jensen. A major milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, a training budget of $15,000 has been approved for the coding team and project managers, with sessions starting next month. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, have been updated and will take effect in January. The project is also associated with 'Zenith Innovations' and a 'Revolutionary AI Project,' with onboarding scheduled for April 15th, 2023."
